      "writtenOn": "2021-05-17T01:37:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your review:)\n\nThe way to make it support pte_special is to define a new bit. The possible available space is between L_PTE_YOUNG and L_PTE_DIRTY,\n\n#define L_PTE_YOUNG\t\t(_AT(pteval_t, 1) \u003c\u003c 1)    //      10b\n#define L_PTE_DIRTY\t\t(_AT(pteval_t, 1) \u003c\u003c 6)    // 1000000b\n                                  //Range for L_PTE_MT_ooo // -oooo--b\n\n\nTo add a newly defined bit into the range, the possible solution is to \"compact\" xxx_mt_table. This table is used to translate Linux version\u0027s PTE to HW PTE.\n\nThe way to compact the table is done by the following 2 methods,\n1. Find out the same HW PTE setting.\n\na. \"PTE_EXT_TEX(1)\"\n.long\tPTE_EXT_TEX(1)\t\t\t\t\t@ L_PTE_MT_BUFFERABLE\n.long\tPTE_EXT_TEX(1)\t\t\t\t\t@ L_PTE_MT_DEV_WC\n\nThey can be merged into one .long field, which means L_PTE_MT_DEV_WC can be defined as L_PTE_MT_BUFFERABLE.\n\nb. \"PTE_CACHEABLE | PTE_BUFFERABLE\"\n.long\tPTE_CACHEABLE | PTE_BUFFERABLE\t\t\t@ L_PTE_MT_WRITEBACK\n.long\tPTE_CACHEABLE | PTE_BUFFERABLE\t\t\t@ L_PTE_MT_DEV_CACHED\n\nAlso, they can be merged.\n\n\n2. Find out \"unused.\"\n\nThere are 2 unused .long fields before the 7th entry (The index to xxx_mt_table is 111b)\n\n.long\t0x00\t\t\t\t\t\t@ unused\n.long\t0x00\t\t\t\t\t\t@ L_PTE_MT_MINICACHE (not present)\n\nSo they can be reserved for L_PTE_MT_VECTORS and L_PTE_MT_DEV_NONSHARED respectively.\n\n\nNow, the number of bits to mention L_PTE_MT_XXX needs 3 bits only.\n\n#define L_PTE_YOUNG\t\t(_AT(pteval_t, 1) \u003c\u003c 1)    //      10b\n#define L_PTE_DIRTY\t\t(_AT(pteval_t, 1) \u003c\u003c 6)    // 1000000b\n                                  //Range for L_PTE_MT_ooo // -xooo--b\n\nSo we can define L_PTE_SPECIAL as\n\n#define L_PTE_SPECIAL\t\t(_AT(pteval_t, 1) \u003c\u003c 5)    //  100000b",
      "parentUuid": "b752fc2e_fcbc1cd3",
